solution_steps:
We begin by finding $f^{-1}(x)$.
To do this, we replace $f(x)$ with $y$ in the equation $f(x)=\frac{24}{x+3}$ and solve for $x$.
\begin{align*}
y &= \frac{24}{x+3} \\
yx + 3y &= 24 \\
yx &= 24 - 3y \\
x &= \frac{24 - 3y}{y}
\end{align*}
So $f^{-1}(x) = \frac{24 - 3x}{x}$.
Next, we substitute this expression for $f^{-1}(x)$ into the equation $g(x) = 3f^{-1}(x)$ to find $g(x)$.
\begin{align*}
g(x) &= 3f^{-1}(x) \\
g(x) &= 3\left(\frac{24 - 3x}{x}\right) \\
g(x) &= \frac{72 - 9x}{x}
\end{align*}
We want to find the value of $x$ that makes $g(x) = 15$.
\begin{align*}
15 &= \frac{72 - 9x}{x} \\
15x &= 72 - 9x \\
24x &= 72 \\
x &= \boxed{3}
\end{align*}
The answer is: 3

