label("C",(0,0),W);
[/asy]

solution_steps:
Let $\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix}.$
Then we have \[\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a \\ d \\ g \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix},\] \[\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} b \\ e \\ h \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix},\] and \[\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} c \\ f \\ i \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.\] Therefore, $\mathbf{M} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 & 7 \\ 3 & 5 & -1 \\ -8 & -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}}.$
The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}2&0&7\3&5&-1\-8&-2&4\end{pmatrix}

