solution_steps:
From the triple angle formula for tangent, we have
\[\tan 3 \theta = \frac{3 \tan \theta - \tan^3 \theta}{1 - 3 \tan^2 \theta}.\]
Since $\tan \theta = 4,$ we have
\begin{align*}
\tan 3 \theta &= \frac{3 \cdot 4 - 4^3}{1 - 3 \cdot 4^2} \\
&= \frac{12 - 64}{1 - 48} \\
&= \frac{-52}{-47} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{52}{47}}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: \frac{52}{47}

